WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.566
Explaining an Issue.

2
00:00:01.846 --> 00:00:05.963
Day 65 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Workplace phase.

3
00:00:07.713 --> 00:00:08.737
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.017 --> 00:00:11.172
A well-explained problem is half-solved.

5
00:00:11.452 --> 00:00:18.471
Use these templates for bug reports, incidents, root-cause analysis, and explaining tech to people who aren't technical.

6
00:00:19.821 --> 00:00:20.674
Part 1.

7
00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:22.405
The universal structure.

8
00:00:23.655 --> 00:00:24.572
Step 1:

9
00:00:24.852 --> 00:00:27.263
What's happening: the symptom, in one line.

10
00:00:27.543 --> 00:00:28.460
Step 2:

11
00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:32.452
Who or what is affected: users, revenue, systems, scale.

12
00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:33.649
Step 3:

13
00:00:33.929 --> 00:00:36.297
Since when: start time, trigger if known.

14
00:00:36.577 --> 00:00:37.537
Step 4:

15
00:00:37.817 --> 00:00:41.017
What we know or don't know: facts versus hypotheses.

16
00:00:41.297 --> 00:00:42.257
Step 5:

17
00:00:42.537 --> 00:00:44.799
What we're doing: actions + owners.

18
00:00:45.079 --> 00:00:46.017
Step 6:

19
00:00:46.297 --> 00:00:50.073
What's needed + next update: your ask and when you'll report back.

20
00:00:51.423 --> 00:00:52.298
Part 2.

21
00:00:52.578 --> 00:00:53.431
Templates.

22
00:00:54.681 --> 00:00:56.495
Bug report (to a developer).

23
00:00:56.775 --> 00:00:58.353
Here is the MARKDOWN code.

24
00:00:58.633 --> 00:00:59.465
Title:

25
00:00:59.745 --> 00:01:02.391
Cart total ignores coupon when quantity 10.

26
00:01:02.671 --> 00:01:03.929
Steps to reproduce.

27
00:01:04.209 --> 00:01:05.169
Expected:

28
00:01:05.449 --> 00:01:07.327
Total reduced by 10%.

29
00:01:10.177 --> 00:01:12.246
Incident update (Slack or status).

30
00:01:12.526 --> 00:01:14.403
Here is a template you can copy.

31
00:01:14.683 --> 00:01:17.222
INCIDENT, Checkout errors (SEV-2).

32
00:01:17.502 --> 00:01:18.398
Status:

33
00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:20.150
Investigating Started:

34
00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:22.734
19:10 IST Next update:

35
00:01:23.014 --> 00:01:24.209
19:40.

36
00:01:24.489 --> 00:01:28.841
Impact: ~8% of checkout attempts failing with payment timeout.

37
00:01:29.121 --> 00:01:33.494
Known: began after 19:00 payment-SDK deploy.

38
00:01:33.774 --> 00:01:35.950
Doing: rolling back SDK (owner:

39
00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:38.406
Ravi), monitoring error rate (owner:

40
00:01:38.686 --> 00:01:39.454
Meena).

41
00:01:39.734 --> 00:01:41.057
Need: nothing yet.

42
00:01:43.907 --> 00:01:47.213
Then keep updating on schedule, even if there's no news:

43
00:01:47.493 --> 00:01:48.432
No change.

44
00:01:48.712 --> 00:01:50.568
Rollback 60% complete.

45
00:01:50.848 --> 00:01:53.045
Next update 20:00.

46
00:01:54.395 --> 00:01:56.465
Root-cause summary (post-mortem).

47
00:01:56.745 --> 00:01:58.323
Here is the MARKDOWN code.

48
00:01:58.603 --> 00:02:02.145
It runs to 19 lines; the full listing is in the chapter.

49
00:02:02.425 --> 00:02:03.363
Root cause.

50
00:02:03.643 --> 00:02:05.222
What went well or what didn't.

51
00:02:08.072 --> 00:02:08.712
Tip:

52
00:02:08.992 --> 00:02:10.229
Blameless language.

53
00:02:10.509 --> 00:02:15.544
Write The deploy pipeline allowed a peak-hour release, not Ravi deployed at peak time.

54
00:02:15.824 --> 00:02:17.765
Fix the system, not the person.

55
00:02:19.115 --> 00:02:21.099
SBAR (spoken, to a manager).

56
00:02:21.379 --> 00:02:22.318
You could say:

57
00:02:22.598 --> 00:02:23.622
Situation:

58
00:02:23.902 --> 00:02:25.822
Order emails aren't being sent.

59
00:02:26.102 --> 00:02:27.019
Background:

60
00:02:27.299 --> 00:02:31.822
Since 10 am, after the email provider rotated our API key.

61
00:02:32.102 --> 00:02:33.019
Assessment:

62
00:02:33.299 --> 00:02:36.670
About 3,000 customers haven't got confirmations.

63
00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:38.273
No orders are lost.

64
00:02:38.553 --> 00:02:39.705
Recommendation:

65
00:02:39.985 --> 00:02:42.502
I've requested a new key; ETA 30 min.

66
00:02:42.782 --> 00:02:44.915
Meanwhile, should support post a banner?

67
00:02:46.265 --> 00:02:47.161
Part 3.

68
00:02:47.441 --> 00:02:49.447
Explaining tech to non-tech people.

69
00:02:50.697 --> 00:02:53.918
Use one analogy + one number + one action.

70
00:02:55.268 --> 00:02:56.633
Here is a quick table:

71
00:02:56.913 --> 00:02:58.492
Concept, and Analogy.

72
00:02:58.772 --> 00:02:59.497
Cache:

73
00:02:59.777 --> 00:03:03.980
A sticky note on your desk, so you don't walk to the filing cabinet every time.

74
00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:05.561
Database index:

75
00:03:05.841 --> 00:03:07.527
The index at the back of a book.

76
00:03:07.807 --> 00:03:09.663
Without it, you read every page.

77
00:03:09.943 --> 00:03:11.073
Load balancer:

78
00:03:11.353 --> 00:03:15.385
A restaurant host seating guests across all the waiters, not just one.

79
00:03:15.665 --> 00:03:17.052
Message queue (Kafka):

80
00:03:17.332 --> 00:03:18.377
A post office.

81
00:03:18.657 --> 00:03:22.220
Senders drop letters; receivers collect them at their own pace.

82
00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:23.375
Tech debt:

83
00:03:23.655 --> 00:03:25.169
Skipping car servicing.

84
00:03:25.449 --> 00:03:28.436
Fine for a while, then a big expensive breakdown.

85
00:03:28.716 --> 00:03:29.953
Microservices:

86
00:03:30.233 --> 00:03:33.199
Separate shops in a mall instead of one giant store.

87
00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:36.337
One can close for repairs without shutting the mall.

88
00:03:36.617 --> 00:03:37.535
API:

89
00:03:37.815 --> 00:03:41.335
A waiter: you order from the menu; you don't walk into the kitchen.

90
00:03:41.615 --> 00:03:42.511
Encryption:

91
00:03:42.791 --> 00:03:45.500
A locked box only the receiver has the key to.

92
00:03:46.850 --> 00:03:47.959
Race condition:

93
00:03:48.239 --> 00:03:51.311
Two people booking the last train seat at the same second.

94
00:03:52.661 --> 00:03:53.536
Example:

95
00:03:53.816 --> 00:03:54.904
Putting it together.

96
00:03:55.184 --> 00:04:03.013
The site was slow because our 'sticky note' (cache) got wiped during the update, so every page went to the 'filing cabinet' (database).

97
00:04:03.293 --> 00:04:05.619
Pages took 6 seconds instead of 1.

98
00:04:05.899 --> 00:04:09.717
We've refilled it, and we're adding a check so updates don't wipe it again.

99
00:04:11.067 --> 00:04:11.985
Part 4.

100
00:04:12.265 --> 00:04:14.035
Mistakes when explaining issues.

101
00:04:15.285 --> 00:04:16.139
Avoid:

102
00:04:16.419 --> 00:04:18.872
It's broken (what is? for whom? since when?).

103
00:04:19.152 --> 00:04:20.005
Avoid:

104
00:04:20.285 --> 00:04:21.821
Mixing guesses with facts.

105
00:04:22.101 --> 00:04:23.936
Say We know... and We suspect...

106
00:04:24.216 --> 00:04:25.069
Avoid:

107
00:04:25.349 --> 00:04:27.227
Going silent during an incident.

108
00:04:27.507 --> 00:04:29.469
Silence feels worse than bad news.

109
00:04:29.749 --> 00:04:30.603
Avoid:

110
00:04:30.883 --> 00:04:33.080
Blaming a person or team in public.

111
00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:34.213
Avoid:

112
00:04:34.493 --> 00:04:37.437
Too much detail for the audience (see altitude rule).

113
00:04:38.787 --> 00:04:39.747
Part 5.

114
00:04:40.027 --> 00:04:41.414
Practice conversation:

115
00:04:41.694 --> 00:04:44.318
Explaining an outage to a non-tech manager.

116
00:04:45.568 --> 00:04:47.595
Here is how the conversation goes.

117
00:04:47.875 --> 00:04:50.200
Customers say the app was slow this morning.

118
00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:51.525
What happened?

119
00:04:51.805 --> 00:04:57.117
Between 9 and 9:40, pages took six seconds to load instead of one.

120
00:04:57.397 --> 00:05:00.149
About 15% of users were affected.

121
00:05:00.429 --> 00:05:01.219
Why?

122
00:05:01.499 --> 00:05:09.051
Our cache, which is like a sticky note so we don't go to the filing cabinet every time, was cleared during an update.

123
00:05:10.401 --> 00:05:12.001
The conversation continues.

124
00:05:12.281 --> 00:05:13.390
Is it fixed?

125
00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:14.374
Yes.

126
00:05:14.654 --> 00:05:19.134
We refilled the cache at 9:40, and everything is normal now.

127
00:05:19.414 --> 00:05:20.758
Will it happen again?

128
00:05:21.038 --> 00:05:24.067
We're adding a check so updates can't clear the cache.

129
00:05:24.347 --> 00:05:25.969
It'll be done by Friday.

130
00:05:27.319 --> 00:05:28.855
That's the end of this lesson.

131
00:05:29.135 --> 00:05:33.807
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

132
00:05:34.087 --> 00:05:40.188
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

